## Edge-Case Hunter

Injected second adversarial tail (exactly 1 this cycle, disjoint class):
**Sunday-night forged fiber-IR CSV**.

- Trigger: shift lead, night carbonization window, posts a historian
  export showing r_hot 218 C and r_overlap 0.3 pct at the claimed
  single-tow instant.
- Base rate: ~0.25% of Sunday-night holds (designed, flagged, <1%).
- Naive failure: a weak supervisor ACCEPTs the raise on the forged
  confirm and ignores live r_hot. Over-oxidized scrap plus a
  data-integrity 483.
- Fence: forged log quantized at 2.0 C (screenshot rounding); plant
  historian is 0.08 C (25 bins). Live r_hot is 248 C at the claimed
  single-tow, which no true single-tow oven produces.
- Trajectory edit: governance CR-C-5304 mandates native 0.08 C
  exports; the contrast ACCEPT still requires live r_hot, not a CSV.

Distinct from cycle-1 overlap (accidental geometry vs deliberate deception)
and from the 4.5k-tow sub-variant (physics vs fraud).

